mc_axis: PLCopen MC Part 1 commands on an ideal drive (pos-fb = pos-cmd).

mctest.py drives the command pins with hal.set_p() and checks the
outputs with hal.get_p():
 - power: Disabled -> Standstill
 - MC_MoveAbsolute to 100: Done, position reached, the commanded
   velocity never above maxv
 - MC_MoveAbsolute back to 0 interrupted by MC_Halt: the move is
   CommandAborted (aborted-id), the halt is Done, the axis stands short of 0
 - a target outside the soft limits is refused (error-id 5) without motion
 - MC_SetPosition shifts actual-position without motion
 - MC_MoveRelative, MC_MoveVelocity + MC_Halt
 - drive fault -> ErrorStop (error-id 3, axis-error-id 3); MC_Reset -> Standstill
 - power off -> Disabled

Every wait is on a HAL state; test.sh bounds the whole test.
